.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"93d6e468b43a71dc8f9e089060403beb5e252613e767c1f3ac8b5187a8c2fcba","event_uuid":"11fb4bc0-ec9d-412d-a8b2-c228ca52be9f","position":{"commit_sha":"518b61e59b2db075d6b2fc6efa9d1fd66327c6d4","position":"1785882963410702001-11fb4bc0-ec9d-412d-a8b2-c228ca52be9f"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"be66ca83f5cdcb0621a7698b070b8edfcd3e834c0be3ad2b69ca00714360c51d","event_uuid":"ff884f20-8b76-4d11-addc-c43ff61071ec","position":{"commit_sha":"ed9095c5ee0283f3b16e9413822b013525c4ad2f","position":"1785883025630407001-ff884f20-8b76-4d11-addc-c43ff61071ec"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED oracle contract: authoritative contract is this ticket's current-history-preference and recorded-SHA fallback ACs, grounded in the disposable rewrite rehearsal. Production path is the real verify-identity CLI over a real temporary tickets Git history. The rewrite case will prove a compacted ledger has non-null old SHAs, rewrite every reachable commit while preserving the exact tip tree, prove each event position resolves to a different current SHA, and require the gate to remain verified. The contrast/fallback case will use an unresolvable current position plus a reachable recorded pre-key SHA and require key-not-valid-at-era, proving the recorded SHA—not a null anchor—is retained. Tier: real-Git subprocess integration in the focused unit module; one tier lower cannot exercise ancestry or history resolution. Gate: the exact pytest nodes under make test. Collateral invariants: ledger schema/event bytes and live-event behavior remain covered by existing tests.","timestamp":1785882963410702001},{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"RED evidence: the real-Git rewrite regression collected and executed under pytest; before rewrite the compacted ledger verified, every stored SHA was non-null, and the exact snapshot bytes were frozen. After recreating every reachable commit with identical trees, each position resolved to the corresponding new SHA, yet the current gate returned four key_not_valid_at_era verdicts and exit 1. The recorded-SHA fallback contrast passed on baseline by design; it is a preservation/negative-control oracle and will be held out to reject a naive overwrite-with-None implementation.","timestamp":1785883025630407001}],"created_at":1785882236245336001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"9c038609-81b5-41cc-a94f-3eae0d360452","relation":"discovered_from","target_id":"561e-e186-a902-461c"},{"link_uuid":"acc72d1c-2128-438d-8ab0-7d670e622987","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"ba2b-2284-5e0c-429a"}],"description":"## Context\n\nThe disposable quiet-window rehearsal for `561e-e186-a902-461c` proved that the history strip preserves tree/commit/merge/pack invariants but violates the required authorship identity invariant. Pre-rewrite `verify-identity` reported 8728 verified and 18 key-not-valid-at-era over 9875 in-scope events. Post-rewrite, with the correctly mapped enforce-since boundary and identical scope, it reported 3133 verified and 5613 key-not-valid-at-era. The cause is compacted authorship-ledger entries retaining their pre-rewrite `position.commit_sha`; the verifier trusts every non-null stored SHA and re-resolves by position only when the stored SHA is null. A commit-history rewrite necessarily changes those SHAs while preserving each event position.\n\n## Plan\n\n- Add a real-Git regression that creates signed events, compacts them into a ledger with non-null commit SHAs, rewrites commit history without changing the ticket tree, and proves the current verifier misclassifies the authentic ledger entry at the new epoch.\n- In the whole-store verifier, treat a ledger `commit_sha` as a cache: when the ledger carries a position, resolve that position against the current tickets history and prefer the current resolved commit; retain the recorded SHA only as the fail-closed fallback when the position cannot be resolved.\n- Add a focused fallback regression with a non-null recorded ledger SHA and a position that the current-history resolver cannot resolve; assert classification still uses the recorded SHA.\n- Preserve live-event behavior, ledger wire format, event bytes, current tree, and the existing null-commit recovery behavior.\n- Re-run the disposable pre/post identity comparison and require identical summary counts plus identical `(event_uuid, verdict, grandfathered)` multisets when `commit` is ignored.\n- Land through Gerrit with `LLM-Review +1`, `Verified +1`, and zero unresolved comments before the maintenance window.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A compacted ledger entry with a non-null pre-rewrite commit SHA is verified against the commit resolved from its position in the current history.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] If current-history position resolution fails, the verifier retains the recorded ledger commit SHA as its fallback.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] Live-event commit resolution and classification are unchanged.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] The authorship-ledger persisted schema and event bytes are unchanged.\n- [ ] [code-verifiable] A real-Git history-rewrite regression preserves the signed event verdict after all commit SHAs change.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The full disposable pre/post identity summaries are identical after the fix.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The full disposable `(event_uuid, verdict, grandfathered)` multisets are identical when rewritten commit SHAs are ignored.\n- [ ] [operator-attested] The Gerrit fix lands with both required positive votes and zero unresolved comments.\n\n## Scope\n\n`src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py` and focused unit/integration tests only. No ticket-store event rewrite, no schema migration, and no authoritative maintenance mutation.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[{"path":"src/rebar/_commands/verify_authorship.py","reason":"re-resolve compacted ledger positions against the current tickets history before era verification"},{"path":"tests/unit/test_identity_gate_scope_and_ledger.py","reason":"real-Git regression for non-null ledger commit SHAs across a history rewrite plus fallback compatibility"}],"file_impact_scope":"paths","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["parent","0303-692c-55dc-4a18"],["relates_to","ba2b-2284-5e0c-429a"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"","parent_id":"0303-692c-55dc-4a18","parent_status_uuid":"760e2359-532b-4220-affe-dca5fe16289e","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":["identity","reclaim"],"ticket_id":"d0f3-2262-4f33-4ebf","ticket_type":"bug","title":"Preserve authorship-era verdicts across tickets history rewrite","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["4c61deb4-fec2-4246-8976-ddfd9f082d14","dd620517-f5a0-4dec-9580-62f28c4b2ff4","9c038609-81b5-41cc-a94f-3eae0d360452","5efdd68f-3bf1-4e2a-a968-